---
description: Build Curv OS screens with page shells from @curvgroup/design-system. Always on for UI work.
globs:
  - "**/*.tsx"
  - "**/*.jsx"
alwaysApply: true
---

This is a Curv OS app. UI comes from `@curvgroup/design-system`.

When the user asks for a screen, pick one shell (they will not name it):

- list / table / queue / catalog → `ListPage`
- one product / deal / customer / SKU → `DetailPage` (verdict + max 4 vitals + tabs)
- overview / dashboard / home → `DashboardPage` (max 5 KPIs, max 2 charts)
- P&L / statement → `ReportPage`
- settings / form → `SettingsPage`

Copy `node_modules/@curvgroup/design-system/examples/<shell>.tsx`. Replace data. Do not add sections. Extra data goes in a tab, drawer, or hover — never a new card on the canvas. Never hand-roll AppFrame, DataTable, or a page layout. Do not invent props.
